Third-party code adapted into crawm
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

crawm deliberately reuses ideas and (where noted) code from the following projects.
Adapted files carry a header comment identifying their origin; this file records the
projects and their licenses.

  * niri            — GPL-3.0-or-later — https://github.com/YaLTeR/niri
  * cosmic-comp     — GPL-3.0-only     — https://github.com/pop-os/cosmic-comp
  * mango           — GPL-3.0-or-later — https://github.com/mangowm/mango
  * smithay         — MIT              — https://github.com/Smithay/smithay
  * anvil (example) — MIT              — https://github.com/Smithay/smithay

See ROADMAP.md §11 and docs/decisions/0001-license.md for details.

Files adapted so far:

  * `src/animation/spring.rs` — the damped-spring solution, adapted from niri's
    `src/animation/spring.rs`, which follows libadwaita's spring animation
    (LGPL-2.1-or-later, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libadwaita) and, behind it,
    RBBAnimation (MIT).
  * `src/animation/curve.rs` — the cubic-Bézier solver follows the same shape as
    niri's `src/animation/bezier.rs` and libadwaita's easing code
    (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

